    {
      "id": "glossary-retired",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Retired words",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Retired words",
        "body": "Words older graphs and pages use, and what replaced them. A current graph never uses them.\n\n- **Declaration**, **manifest** — the root.\n- **View** — a face. **View sequence** — next-face.\n- **landing surface** — the ground.\n- **Field** — a Property.\n- **Markdown node** — Content with kind `markdown`.\n- **Bridge node** — an import or an export. The Bridge is the connection between them.\n- **Graph Reference** — a Portal.\n- **groups** — rooting.\n- **frame**, **border**, **wrap** (for a graph's boundary) — the Membrane.\n- **handle** (in a file) — a Port. \"Handle\" is only the spot you grab on screen, and is never saved.\n- **Event Handler**, **Script** — leaving in favour of Methods and the `invokes` edge.",
